From fe8bc4bfb046e6ffc8922c7f5f6ea9483a6ce037 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:51:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Review of 2aeac71: replaced copy, sent hash, mined notes,
 stricter dependency check, NODE_ENV

- TRANSACTION_REPLACED copy no longer claims "not credited" nor names a button that may be hidden: the
  payment did not complete as sent; do not pay again; a real payment is still reconciled at finality.
- The wallet state keeps the hash an intent was sent with (sentHash); the panel drops a failed
  payment's note by it, not by a pasted replacement hash.
- A note the wallet saw mined (confirmed, payment step) is marked and kept past the after-expiry
  margin (a late-mined payment or a slow indexer is still on its way); only the 2 h cap ends it.
- deploy.mjs: a missing/unreadable or pre-v2 lockfile, or a node_modules not installed by npm ci, is a
  refusal, not a pass; a same-version package from another source (resolved/integrity) is refused; an
  absent devOptional package for another platform is fine; NODE_ENV other than production is refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
